  "notes": [
    "COHERENCE (2026-10-22): ch1 is one rainy night at one harbor, walked west to east: a0 WASSOON HARBOR is the sea-wall road (E4a0 352-1024 only), a1 THE JAIL QUAY is the row of quay sheds behind it (E6a0 0-832 only: plank sheds and brick), a2 THE HARBOR GATE is the stone jail quay at the water where the prison barge loads (E8a1 96-1376 only: cell doors, wall shackles, torches, the harbor water at the foot of the wall). Each area walks back and forth through its one source strip (every leg <= 512 px, leftward legs mirrored), so every join is a mirror join or a continuation and the scenery never jumps between unrelated places; the place changes only at the two fades.",
    "Palette: harbor-night on every slice (night scale, pens 1-3 kept for lamp and window glow, 20% toward #1a2a5a on every row); s3ops on the far layer. One far layer for the whole chapter: the E4a0 bay (sea, fortress domes, the far city) behind the sea wall, over the shed roofs and through the quay arches.",
    "Test-safe start (gate 3): the E4a0 pavement is widened toward the sea wall under every slice of a0 (E4a0 floor cells h 16-64 copied to y 112 with their terrain), so the lane 113-224 is floor art and flat over the first 640 px.",
    "a2 lane: the E8a1 quay ledge (rows y 128-192, floor art) is walk-patched onto the wading strip below it, lane 129-224.",
    "Boss arena (1-6, WARDEN ROOK, the dock jailer with the boat hook and rope): the quay is rigged for loading the barge: crane masts (E6a0 lattice towers, lifted), hanging chains with hooks (E8a1 shackles, lifted), the barge's iron cell doors; the runtime adds the crane set piece and its shadow."
  ],
